skill: "retrospective-synthesis"
sections[3]:
  - "# retrospective-synthesis\n\nConvert a sprint retrospective into evidence-linked actions. Use at sprint end, after an incident, or whenever velocity or burndown moves without an obvious cause. Clusters the transcript into themes, ties each theme to a delivery metric, and caps the action list at what the team can actually carry.\n\nOwner: role-scrum-agile-coach (pod-build, product). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"retro transcript retro-transcript.toon; sprint metrics sprint-metrics.toon (velocity, burndown leakage, cycle time, WIP); prior retro actions retro-actions.toon\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/product/retro-synthesis.toon with themes[], actions[] each carrying owner, due metric and check; updated retro-actions.toon\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Read the transcript and the sprint metrics side by side; the retrospective is about this sprint's evidence, not general sentiment.\n2. Cluster transcript notes into themes; discard themes that no participant can tie to a concrete event or metric.\n3. For each surviving theme, attach the metric evidence: velocity delta, burndown leakage days, cycle-time shift or WIP peak that shows the effect.\n4. Check prior retro-actions.toon first; a recurring theme with an already-open action is an escalation (the previous action failed), not a new action.\n5. Propose at most three actions; every action names one owner role, one due metric and one check that will show whether it worked.\n6. Reject actions that restate the theme ('communicate more') with no measurable check.\n7. Emit ask_question when an action needs a decision outside the team's authority, naming the decision holder.\n8. Write retro-synthesis.toon and update retro-actions.toon with status open; close nothing here - closure happens next sprint against the checks.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nactions into next sprint backlog; metric checks into sprint-metrics.toon.\n"
